# CodeCartographer workspace gitignore.
#
# This fork COMMITS the analysis findings, phase handoffs, and amendments so the
# reverse-engineering record is preserved in the repository. The upstream
# template ignores them by default ("generated per-project, can be large");
# this fork opts in to tracking them.
#
# Still machine-local and never committed:
#   - workflow/.orchestrator.local.yaml  (absolute Pi session paths)
#   - workflow/.usage.local.yaml         (timestamps, token counts, absolute paths)
#   - dashboard.html                     (surfaces data from .usage.local.yaml)
#   - .dashboard-narration.local.md      (LLM-narrated summary cache)

# Scratch working notes: handoffs and amendments are committed; other scratch
# notes stay local.
scratch/*
!scratch/.gitkeep
!scratch/handoffs/
!scratch/amendments/

# Orchestrator session pointer (machine-local, written by /codecarto-init
# when run from the Pi extension; the MCP path doesn't write it). Contains
# absolute paths into the user's Pi session storage, so it must never be
# committed.
workflow/.orchestrator.local.yaml

# Phase-run usage log (machine-local, written by /codecarto-next on each
# phase completion; consumed by /codecarto-usage). Holds timestamps, token
# counts, and absolute Pi session-file paths; useless to share, includes
# local cwd metadata, must never be committed.
workflow/.usage.local.yaml

# Generated HTML dashboard. This fork COMMITS it as a useful visual tool.
# The upstream template ignores it because, under the Pi extension, it surfaces
# data from workflow/.usage.local.yaml (absolute Pi session paths). In this
# MCP-driven run the usage log carries no paths (recorded_by: mcp-complete,
# zero tokens/durations), so the dashboard is self-contained and safe to share.
# If a future Pi-extension run writes absolute paths into .usage.local.yaml,
# re-ignore this file before committing.
# dashboard.html

# LLM-narrated executive summary cache (produced by
# /codecarto-dashboard --narrate; preserved across deterministic re-renders
# until the next --narrate).
.dashboard-narration.local.md

# OS artifacts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
